tinycc, the Tiny C Compiler, is a git submodule at third_party/tinycc from
https://github.com/TinyCC/tinycc.git (the mirror of the repository of
Fabrice Bellard and the tinycc developers), at the commit recorded in
this repository's index, release 0.9.28rc. The compiler is under the GNU
Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 (COPYING in the submodule).

Nothing in the submodule is modified. user/Makefile compiles tcc.c as one
source with the configuration on the command line (config.h is empty),
builds the runtime library libtcc1.a from lib/ with the cross compiler,
and installs the compiler's own headers from include/. The files are
exempt from the minios line count and naming conventions. See
docs/design/tcc.md.
